history.log
===========
PROJECT: TunOrient – Orientation & Recommendation Platform
TYPE: AI-assisted full-stack development (FastAPI + React)
HISTORY.LOG — TunOrient Web Services Project

[Phase 1 — Idea Crystallization]
• Prompt: I have an idea but don’t know how to value it in Tunisia. Students have no exposure to orientation before the baccalaureate.
  → Response: AI helped frame the problem as an orientation information gap and suggested a web service focused on guidance, not application handling.

• Prompt: Can we make something about this?
  → Response: Proposed an orientation support platform centered on students, universities, and ministry data.

• Major Direction Change:
  → Project scope clarified as “decision support for orientation”, not managing official applications.

--------------------------------------------------

[Phase 2 — Recommendation Engine Concept]
• Prompt: You mentioned a recommendation engine. What is it in reality and how can I develop it?
  → Response: Explained recommendation engines conceptually (rule-based vs AI-based) and suggested starting with a simple rule-based engine.

• Prompt: If I want to include an AI model, how can the recommendation engine be?
  → Response: AI suggested starting simple (rules, scoring, thresholds) and leaving ML models for future versions.

• Major Direction Change:
  → Recommendation system became a **core objective** of the project.

--------------------------------------------------

[Phase 3 — Scope, Users, and Versioning]
• Prompt: I want to narrow my vision. What should I work on exactly?
  → Response: Defined backend-first approach: database + API + recommendation logic; frontend optional/minimal.

• Prompt: Who are the users of this API?
  → Response: Identified students, universities, and ministry as main stakeholders.

• Prompt: Can universities and ministry be users?
  → Response: Clarified distinction between “users” (authenticated roles) and “data entities”.

• Major Direction Change:
  → Introduced role-based access control (RBAC).

--------------------------------------------------

[Phase 4 — Tunisian Orientation System Corrections]
• Prompt: Explanation of Tunisian reorientation (réorientation sur dossier / examen).
  → Response: AI adjusted system understanding based on user corrections.

• Prompt: My API will NOT handle orientation or reorientation applications.
  → Response: API repositioned as an informational and recommendation service only.

• Major Direction Change:
  → Removed application handling entirely from scope.

--------------------------------------------------

[Phase 5 — Database Design Focus]
• Prompt: I am most concerned about the database. I don’t know what it should include.
  → Response: AI proposed normalized entities (Student, Program, Institution, University, AdmissionRule, OrientationResult, Circular).

• Prompt: Can you give me a PlantUML database diagram?
  → Response: Provided ready-to-use PlantUML ER diagram.

• Prompt: How are updates from universities/ministry handled?
  → Response: Introduced authenticated roles with update rights instead of manual updates.

--------------------------------------------------

[Phase 6 — API Endpoints & RBAC]
• Prompt: Can you explain the endpoints?
  → Response: Detailed explanation of each endpoint and its purpose.

• Prompt: Help me explain role-based access to Copilot.
  → Response: Simplified RBAC rules (student vs ministry/admin) with clear endpoint mapping.

• Major Direction Change:
  → RBAC enforced as a key architectural feature.

--------------------------------------------------

[Phase 7 — Testing & Insomnia]
• Prompt: I want to test in Insomnia but I am lost.
  → Response: Step-by-step Insomnia guide with folders, headers, tokens, and JSON bodies.

• Prompt: Error 405 Method Not Allowed / Timeout in Insomnia.
  → Response: Explained HTTP methods, server status, and common Insomnia mistakes.

--------------------------------------------------

[Phase 8 — Debugging & Backend Fixes]
• Prompt: Uvicorn error about missing UserLogin schema.
  → Response: Identified schema mismatch and fixed auth schemas.

• Prompt: Internal Server Error on login.
  → Response: Debug guidance (logs, hashing, JWT generation).

--------------------------------------------------

[Phase 9 — Frontend Preparation]
• Prompt: npm ENOENT error.
  → Response: Diagnosed Windows npm path issue and provided step-by-step fix.

• Direction:
  → Frontend postponed until backend + API testing are stable.

--------------------------------------------------

[Final Project State]
• Backend: FastAPI + SQLite
• Core Feature: Recommendation Engine for orientation decision support
• Scope: Informational + advisory (NO application handling)
• Key Concepts: RBAC, database design, API versioning, real Tunisian system alignment

END OF LOG

