1. Project Context

Project Name: TunOrient
Type: RESTful Web Service (API-first)
Domain: Academic Orientation & Reorientation in Tunisia
Objective:
Design and implement a backend system that centralizes orientation data and provides rule-based academic recommendations for Tunisian students.

The system serves multiple stakeholders:

Students (pre-baccalaureate & baccalaureate)

Universities & institutions

Ministry of Higher Education

Third-party developers (via API)

2. System Architecture (High-Level)

Architecture Style: RESTful API (client–server)

Backend: Single backend service exposing JSON APIs

Database: Relational (PostgreSQL)

Access: API consumed by future web/mobile apps

Authentication: Basic JWT (optional first version)

3. Core Functional Scope
Students

Create and manage student profiles

Submit baccalaureate average and academic info

Receive orientation/reorientation recommendations

Universities & Institutions

Provide academic programs

Define admission conditions

Ministry of Higher Education

Publish:

Admission rules

Orientation & reorientation circulars

Important deadlines and regulatory updates

Recommendation Engine

Rule-based logic using:

Bac average

Admission thresholds

Program eligibility rules

Store results for traceability

4. Database Model (Relational)
Core Entities

Student

id (PK)

academic_level

specialization

region

bac_average

University

id (PK)

name

region

Institution

id (PK)

name

university_id (FK)

Program

id (PK)

name

institution_id (FK)

capacity

min_score

AdmissionRule

id (PK)

program_id (FK)

min_average

bac_type

year

OrientationResult

id (PK)

student_id (FK)

program_id (FK)

score

decision

created_at

MinistryCircular

id (PK)

title

description

deadline

target_level

published_at

5. Entity Relationships

One University → many Institutions

One Institution → many Programs

One Program → many AdmissionRules

One Student → many OrientationResults

Ministry publishes AdmissionRules and Circulars

6. REST API Design
Main Resources & Endpoints

Students

POST   /students
GET    /students/{id}
PUT    /students/{id}
DELETE /students/{id}


Universities / Institutions

GET /universities
GET /institutions


Programs

GET /programs
GET /programs/{id}


Admission Rules

GET /admission-rules
POST /admission-rules


Recommendations

POST /recommendations/{studentId}
GET  /recommendations/{studentId}


Ministry Circulars

GET  /circulars
POST /circulars

7. Recommendation Logic (Rule-Based)

Basic algorithm:

Retrieve student bac average

Retrieve programs + admission rules

Filter programs where:

student.bac_average >= admission_rule.min_average


Rank results

Store results in OrientationResult

Return recommended programs

No AI — pure rule-based logic aligned with official regulations

8. Technical Constraints

JSON only

REST standards

Proper HTTP status codes

Swagger/OpenAPI documentation required

Clean layered architecture:

Controller

Service

Repository

Entity/Model

9. Expected Deliverables

Fully working REST API

PostgreSQL schema

Swagger documentation

ERD + UML diagrams

Rule-based recommendation engine

Ministry integration (rules + circulars)

10. Development Priorities (Order)

Database schema

Student CRUD

Program & AdmissionRule CRUD

Recommendation logic

Ministry circulars

Swagger documentation

Basic testing

11. Academic Constraints

Focus on backend & architecture

Frontend is optional

Emphasis on:

Data modeling

API design

Clean structure

Real Tunisian context

