How to test with Insomnia (quick steps)
1. Start the server (uvicorn as above).
2. Open Insomnia and create a new request collection.
3. Obtain a JWT:
   - Create a POST request to the auth token/login endpoint (check /docs for exact path; likely /api/v1/auth or /api/v1/auth/token).
   - Body (JSON) example:
     {
       "username": "admin@example.com",
       "password": "password"
     }
   - Send → copy access_token from response (look for {"access_token": "...", "token_type":"bearer"}).
4. Add the Authorization header to protected requests:
   - Header: Authorization
   - Value: Bearer <paste_token_here>
5. Test endpoints:
   - Create student: POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/students  (use JSON body per schema in /docs)
   - Request recommendations: POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/recommendations/{studentId}
   - View programs: GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/programs
6. Use the OpenAPI docs at /docs to confirm exact request/response schemas and endpoints before composing Insomnia requests.

Quick curl equivalents (for copying into Insomnia examples)
- Login:
  curl -X POST "http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/auth/login" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d "{\"username\":\"admin@example.com\",\"password\":\"password\"}"
- Use token:
  curl -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>" http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/programs

Where to check DB path and file
- Open config.py (or .env) to see DATABASE_URL (for SQLite it will be like sqlite:///./data.db). The physical file will be created relative to the project root (e.g., c:\Users\Administrateur\TunOrient\data.db).

