  - region: geographic region.
- How it’s used
  - Reference for institutions; used when listing universities or filtering institutions/programs by region/university.
- Typical queries
  - List all universities: SELECT * FROM universities;
  - Get university + institutions (join): SELECT u.*, i.* FROM universities u JOIN institutions i ON i.university_id = u.id WHERE u.id = ?;
- Suggestions
  - Add UNIQUE(name) if names should be unique.
  - Index region for region-based filters.
  - FK on institutions: ForeignKey("universities.id", ondelete="RESTRICT") or CASCADE depending on policy.

Institution
- Purpose
  - Represents an institution (faculty/college) that belongs to a university and holds programs.
- Fields
  - id (PK): institution identifier.
  - name: institution name.
  - university_id (FK): references universities.id.
- How it’s used
  - Parent for programs; used to show which university a program belongs to and to filter programs/institutions.
- Typical queries
  - List institutions for a university: SELECT * FROM institutions WHERE university_id = ?;
  - Get institution + programs: SELECT i.*, p.* FROM institutions i JOIN programs p ON p.institution_id = i.id WHERE i.id = ?;
- Suggestions
  - UNIQUE(university_id, name) to prevent duplicate institution names within same university.
  - Index university_id.
  - FK on university with ondelete="CASCADE" only if you want institutions removed when a university is deleted — else RESTRICT.

Program
- Purpose
  - Stores study programs students can be recommended to (degree/field/capacity).
- Fields
  - id (PK)
  - name
  - degree (e.g., Licence, Master)
  - field (study field)
  - capacity (int)
  - min_score (float) — optional program-level threshold
  - institution_id (FK) — which institution offers it
- How it’s used
  - Matched against AdmissionRule and student scores; returned in recommendations and listings.
- Typical queries
  - List programs by institution/field: SELECT * FROM programs WHERE institution_id = ?;
  - Join rules: SELECT p.*, r.* FROM programs p LEFT JOIN admission_rules r ON r.program_id = p.id WHERE p.id = ?;
- Suggestions
  - Indexes: institution_id, field.
  - UNIQUE(institution_id, name) if program names are unique per institution.
  - Keep both program.min_score and admission_rules to allow program-level hints and rule overrides.
  - Add FK constraint with ondelete=RESTRICT to protect historical OrientationResult rows, or CASCADE if you prefer cleanup.

AdmissionRule
- Purpose
  - Encodes eligibility rules for a program (min_average, bac_type, year etc.). Multiple rules per program supported.
- Fields
  - id (PK)
  - program_id (FK)
  - min_average (float): required minimum bac average
  - bac_type (string): stream/type (if rules differ by bac stream)
  - year (string): academic year or cohort
- How it’s used
  - Core input to recommendation engine: student.bac_average >= min_average (and bac_type matches) → eligible.
  - Admins/ministry create/update these rules.
- Typical queries
  - Rules for program: SELECT * FROM admission_rules WHERE program_id = ?;
  - All rules for year/type: SELECT * FROM admission_rules WHERE year = ? AND bac_type = ?;
- Suggestions
  - Index program_id, (year), (bac_type) if commonly filtered.
  - Consider composite uniqueness e.g., UNIQUE(program_id, bac_type, year) to prevent duplicate rules.
  - Enforce min_average >= 0 and <= 20 (or local BAC scale) with application validation.

Student
- Purpose
  - Holds student profile and academic data used by the recommendation engine.
- Fields
  - id (PK)
  - academic_level (string) — e.g., "pre-bac" / "baccalaureate"
  - specialization / bac_stream (string)
  - region (string)
  - bac_average (float)
- How it’s used
  - Input to recommendations; used to display profile and historical orientation results.
- Typical queries
  - Fetch student profile: SELECT * FROM students WHERE id = ?;
  - Filter students by region/average for reporting: SELECT * FROM students WHERE region = ? AND bac_average >= ?;
- Suggestions
  - Index bac_average and region for analytics.
  - If you have authentication, separate auth User table (id, email, hashed_password, role) and link Student.user_id → users.id.
  - Validate bac_average range at schema level.

OrientationResult (already provided; short summary)
- Purpose
  - Stores the outcome of a recommendation run per (student, program) for traceability and auditing.
- Fields recap
  - id, student_id (FK), program_id (FK), score, decision, created_at (timestamp)
- How it’s used
  - Persisted when recommendations run; returned to students and admins for history and appeals.
- Suggestions
  - Index student_id, program_id, created_at.
  - Add run_id (grouping), reason/explanation field, and program relationship for easier joins.
  - Choose ondelete behavior carefully to preserve audit trail (usually RESTRICT).

MinisterialCircular (MinisterialCircular / MinistryCircular)
- Purpose
  - Stores official circulars: deadlines, published rules, announcements targeted at students/universities.
- Fields
  - id (PK)
  - title
  - description (text)
  - deadline (datetime) — last valid date
  - target_level (string) — who it targets (e.g., "Baccalaureate", "Licence")
  - published_at (datetime)
- How it’s used
  - Displayed to students and institutions; used to enforce deadlines and inform the recommendation engine/admins.
- Typical queries
  - Active circulars: SELECT * FROM ministerial_circulars WHERE deadline >= CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
  - Latest circulars: SELECT * FROM ministerial_circulars ORDER BY published_at DESC LIMIT 10;
- Suggestions
  - Index published_at and deadline.
  - Consider storing attachment URLs or versioning if circulars get updated.
  - Restrict POST/PUT to ministry/admin roles.

Cross-table / System-level suggestions
- FK & ondelete: Prefer RESTRICT for historical tables (OrientationResult) to preserve records; CASCADE for pure dependent data when appropriate.
- Indexing: Add indexes on common filter columns (student_id, program_id, institution_id, university_id, created_at, region).
- Uniqueness & constraints: Use UNIQUE where business rules require (e.g., no duplicate institution names within a university, no duplicate admission rule per program+bac_type+year).
- Audit / provenance: Add created_by / updated_by columns (user id) on sensitive tables (AdmissionRule, MinisterialCircular, OrientationResult.run_by) for accountability.
- Referential integrity: Use proper FK constraints in SQLAlchemy Column(ForeignKey(..., ondelete=...)) and configure relationship(cascade=...) per desired behavior.
- Migrations: Use Alembic to manage schema changes safely (especially for production).

If you want, I can:
- Generate updated SQLAlchemy model code that includes suggested indexes, FKs with ondelete, and relationships (ready to drop into app/models/models.py).
- Or scaffold routers/schemas for each table to match the endpoints list. Which next step do you prefer?

