Short answer: run your FastAPI app with uvicorn and use the server URL (http://127.0.0.1:8000) + your API prefix (usually /api/v1) as the base URL in Insomnia. Do NOT use flask run (that is for Flask apps).

Exact step‑by‑step (Windows PowerShell) — minimal and complete

1) Start the server (from project root)
```powershell
# activate venv (adjust name if you used 'venv' instead of '.venv')
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1

# start uvicorn (use this exact command)
python -m uvicorn app.main:app --reload --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000
```

2) Verify address shown by uvicorn
- Look for the line: Uvicorn running on http://127.0.0.1:8000
- Open in browser to confirm:
  - Swagger UI: http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs
  - Redoc: http://127.0.0.1:8000/redoc

3) Determine API base URL
- If you registered routers under prefix "/api/v1" (app.include_router(api_router, prefix="/api/v1")), the API base is:
  http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1
- If unsure, open /docs and copy the server + path shown for endpoints.

4) Create Insomnia workspace & environment
- Open Insomnia → Create New Workspace → name: TunOrient.
- Manage Environments → add variables:
  - base_url = "http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1"
  - token = ""  (leave blank until you login)

5) Create requests in Insomnia (examples)
- Auth → Login (POST)
  - URL: {{ base_url }}/auth/login
  - Body: JSON per your auth schema (or form if using OAuth2PasswordRequestForm)
  - Send → copy access_token from response

- Store token in environment
  - Edit env.token = <access_token>

- Protected request header template
  - Add header to protected requests:
    Authorization: Bearer {{ token }}

- Example resource requests
  - Create student: POST {{ base_url }}/students  (JSON body: academic_level, bac_average, etc.)
  - Get programs: GET {{ base_url }}/programs
  - Run recommendations: POST {{ base_url }}/recommendations/{student_id}
  - Get recommendations: GET {{ base_url }}/recommendations/{student_id}

6) Quick curl examples (useful to paste into Insomnia docs)
```bash
# login (example)
curl -X POST "http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/auth/login" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"username":"user","password":"pass"}'

# create student (with token)
curl -X POST "http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/students" -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"academic_level":"baccalaureate","bac_average":14.5}'
```

7) Troubleshooting
- If uvicorn not running: ensure venv activated and required packages installed (pip install -r requirements.txt).
- If /docs returns 404: server not running or your API prefix is different — check main.py for include_router prefix.
- 401 on protected endpoints: ensure Authorization header is exactly: Bearer <token>.
- If you changed host/port, update base_url accordingly (http://localhost:PORT/...).

If you want, I can produce an Insomnia export (collection + env) with these example requests ready to import. Which format do you prefer?

