ons-said: Project Completion Instructions (What to Add / Modify)

This backend is an academic orientation platform. Some core concepts are missing or incorrectly implemented. Please apply the following changes step by step.

1️⃣ Add a Dedicated University Domain
Missing items:

There is no clear separation between universities, institutions, and programs in the API.

What to add:

Create a universities feature:

GET /api/v1/universities

GET /api/v1/universities/{id}

POST /api/v1/universities

Create an institutions feature linked to universities:

GET /api/v1/institutions

GET /api/v1/institutions/{id}

POST /api/v1/institutions

Programs must belong to an institution, not be standalone.

2️⃣ Add Ministry-Controlled Resources

There is an important actor missing: the Ministry of Higher Education.

What to add:

A ministerial_circulars resource:

GET /api/v1/circulars

GET /api/v1/circulars/{id}

POST /api/v1/circulars

Circulars contain:

title

academic year

publication date

deadline date

Only ministry/admin roles can create or update these.

3️⃣ Fix Orientation Logic (Very Important)

Orientation results must NOT be managed as normal CRUD data.

What is wrong:

Orientation results currently have POST, PUT, and DELETE

This implies users manually create recommendations, which is incorrect

What to change:

Remove:

POST /orientations

PUT /orientations/{id}

DELETE /orientations/{id}

Keep only:

GET /orientations/{student_id}

Add instead:

POST /recommendations/{student_id}
→ This endpoint generates orientation results automatically using business logic

Orientation results are system-generated outputs, not user inputs.

4️⃣ Add Admission Rules Management

Orientation decisions must rely on official eligibility rules.

What to add:

A dedicated admission_rules resource:

GET /api/v1/admission-rules

POST /api/v1/admission-rules

Admission rules include:

bac stream

minimum score

academic year

These rules are used internally by the recommendation engine.

Only ministry/admin users can modify these rules.

5️⃣ Add Recommendation Engine Service

Orientation logic must be isolated in a service layer.

What to implement:

A RecommendationService that:

Reads student data

Filters programs by admission rules

Computes score gap

Generates eligibility status

Saves results automatically

The API layer should only call this service — no logic inside routes.

6️⃣ Add Role Awareness (Student vs Ministry)

Even if roles are basic for now:

Students:

Read recommendations

Read universities, programs, circulars

Ministry/Admin:

Manage admission rules

Manage circulars

Manage universities & institutions

Enforce this gradually using dependency injection or guards.

7️⃣ Keep Authentication As Is

Auth endpoints (login, register) are fine and should not be modified now.

8️⃣ Naming & Structure Rules to Follow

Use plural resource names

REST endpoints describe resources, not actions

Business logic must never be in routers

Generated data ≠ CRUD data

✅ Final Goal

After these changes:

The system becomes rule-driven

Orientation becomes traceable and explainable

The platform matches real academic orientation workflows

