Base info
- Server base URL (development): http://127.0.0.1:8000
- API prefix used in this project: /api/v1
- Full base for requests: http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1
- Swagger UI (explore requests / schemas): http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs
- Auth: obtain Bearer token from POST /api/v1/auth/login and send header Authorization: Bearer <token> for protected endpoints.

Below is a concise, complete endpoint reference with exact usage, required auth/roles, example request bodies and expected response codes.

1) Auth
- POST /api/v1/auth/register
  - Purpose: create a new user
  - Body (JSON):
    ````json
    {"email":"user@example.com","password":"Secret123","role":"student"}
    ````
  - Response: 201 Created → UserRead (id, email, role, is_active)
  - No auth required.

- POST /api/v1/auth/login
  - Purpose: log in and receive JWT access token
  - Body (JSON):
    ````json
    {"email":"user@example.com","password":"Secret123"}
    ````
  - Response: 200 OK → {"access_token":"<jwt>","token_type":"bearer"}
  - Use this token in Authorization header for protected routes.

2) Students
- POST /api/v1/students
  - Purpose: create a student record
  - Body example:
    ````json
    {
      "academic_level":"baccalaureate",
      "specialization":"Math",
      "region":"Tunis",
      "bac_average":15.2
    }
    ````
  - Response: 201 Created → StudentRead
  - Currently not role-restricted (no auth dependency present).

- GET /api/v1/students/{student_id}
  - Purpose: read a student
  - Response: 200 OK → StudentRead or 404 Not Found

- PUT /api/v1/students/{student_id}
  - Purpose: update student fields
  - Body: StudentUpdate (partial fields)
  - Response: 200 OK → StudentRead or 404

- DELETE /api/v1/students/{student_id}
  - Purpose: delete student
  - Response: 204 No Content or 404

- GET /api/v1/students/
  - Purpose: list students
  - Response: 200 OK → list[StudentRead]
  - Note: current implementation had a bug in list_all; if list returns server error, open router.py and service.list_all to fix repository call.

3) Orientations (read-only results)
- GET /api/v1/orientations/{student_id}
  - Purpose: retrieve system-generated orientation results (orientation_results) for a student
  - Auth: Requires valid JWT (any authenticated user)
  - Response: 200 OK → list[OrientationResultRead] (program_id, score, decision, created_at)

  Usage example (curl):
  ```bash
  curl -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>" http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/orientations/1
  ```

4) Recommendations (engine)
- POST /api/v1/recommendations/{student_id}
  - Purpose: run the recommendation engine for a student; service generates OrientationResult rows and returns them
  - Auth: Requires valid JWT (any authenticated user). Role guards can be added if needed.
  - Response: 200 OK → list[OrientationResultRead]
  - Example:
    ```bash
    curl -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>" http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/recommendations/1
    ```

5) Universities
- GET /api/v1/universities
  - Purpose: list universities
  - Response: 200 OK → list[UniversityRead]

- GET /api/v1/universities/{id}
  - Purpose: get a single university
  - Response: 200 OK → UniversityRead or 404

- POST /api/v1/universities
  - Purpose: create a university
  - Body:
    ````json
    {"name":"University of X","region":"Sfax"}
    ````
  - Auth/Role: Requires ministry or admin role (dependency require_role("ministry","admin"))
  - Response: 201 Created → UniversityRead

6) Institutions (linked to universities)
- GET /api/v1/institutions
  - Response: 200 OK → list[InstitutionRead]

- GET /api/v1/institutions/{id}
  - Response: 200 OK → InstitutionRead or 404

- POST /api/v1/institutions
  - Body:
    ````json
    {"name":"Engineering School","university_id":1}
    ````
  - Auth/Role: ministry or admin required
  - Response: 201 Created → InstitutionRead

7) Programs (belong to institutions)
- GET /api/v1/programs
  - Response: 200 OK → list[ProgramRead]

- GET /api/v1/programs/{id}
  - Response: 200 OK → ProgramRead or 404

- POST /api/v1/programs
  - Body example:
    ````json
    {
      "name":"Computer Science",
      "degree":"Licence",
      "field":"Informatics",
      "capacity":120,
      "institution_id":2
    }
    ````
  - Auth/Role: ministry or admin required
  - Response: 201 Created → ProgramRead

8) Admission Rules (used by recommendation engine)
- GET /api/v1/admission-rules
  - Purpose: list all admission rules
  - Response: 200 OK → list[AdmissionRuleRead]

- POST /api/v1/admission-rules
  - Body:
    ````json
    {"program_id":3,"bac_stream":"Math","min_score":12.5,"academic_year":"2025"}
    ````
  - Auth/Role: ministry or admin required
  - Response: 201 Created → AdmissionRuleRead

9) Ministerial Circulars (ministry-controlled announcements)
- GET /api/v1/circulars
  - Response: 200 OK → list[CircularRead]

- GET /api/v1/circulars/{id}
  - Response: 200 OK → CircularRead or 404

- POST /api/v1/circulars
  - Body example:
    ````json
    {
      "title":"Admission Circular 2025",
      "academic_year":"2025",
      "publication_date":"2025-06-01T00:00:00",
      "deadline_date":"2025-08-01T00:00:00",
      "description":"Rules and deadlines..."
    }
    ````
  - Auth/Role: ministry or admin required
  - Response: 201 Created → CircularRead

Authentication & role details
- Obtain JWT: POST /api/v1/auth/login → use returned access_token.
- Send header: Authorization: Bearer <access_token>
- Protected endpoints that require authenticated user: /orientations/*, /recommendations/*, and POST circulars (also POST universities/institutions/programs/admission-rules require specific roles).
- Role-enforced endpoints use require_role("ministry","admin") dependency; user.role must match.

