ons-said: Implement a simple role-based access control (RBAC) system.
Roles are limited to student, ministry, and admin.
RBAC is used only to protect data creation and updates, not to manage workflows or applications.

🧩 Student role rules

Users with role student:

can read all public resources (universities, programs, admission rules, circulars)

can create and update their own student profile

can run the recommendation engine

cannot create, update, or delete official data

This means:

students → GET endpoints

students → recommendation endpoints

students → profile endpoints

🧩 Ministry role rules

Users with role ministry:

can create and update universities, institutions, programs

can create and update admission rules

can publish ministerial circulars

cannot access or modify student profiles

cannot submit orientation choices

Ministry users only touch official reference data.

🧩 Admin role rules

Users with role admin:

have full access to all protected endpoints

can perform the same actions as ministry users

are responsible for system maintenance and data imports

Admin ≈ Ministry + technical privileges.

🧩 How RBAC should be enforced (important for Copilot)

RBAC should be enforced using a dependency or middleware that checks user.role.
Use a helper such as require_role("ministry", "admin") to protect sensitive endpoints.
RBAC should be coarse-grained, not fine-grained.

⚠️ Tell Copilot not to:

implement complex permission tables

implement ACLs

implement per-field permissions

