GitHub Copilot: GitHub Copilot

Absolutely! To create a **beautiful landing page** that showcases all your API services, you can add a new component like `LandingPage.js` and make it your default route.

Here’s a simple, modern example using plain CSS (you can later enhance it with a UI library like Material-UI or Ant Design):

---

**src/components/Layout/LandingPage.js**
```javascript
import React from "react";
import { Link } from "react-router-dom";
import "./LandingPage.css";

export default function LandingPage() {
  return (
    <div className="landing-container">
      <h1>Welcome to TunOrient</h1>
      <p>Your gateway to orientation, universities, programs, and more!</p>
      <div className="landing-links">
        <Link to="/students" className="landing-card">👩‍🎓 Students</Link>
        <Link to="/universities" className="landing-card">🏛️ Universities</Link>
        <Link to="/institutions" className="landing-card">🏫 Institutions</Link>
        <Link to="/programs" className="landing-card">📚 Programs</Link>
        <Link to="/admission-rules" className="landing-card">📄 Admission Rules</Link>
        <Link to="/circulars" className="landing-card">📢 Circulars</Link>
        <Link to="/login" className="landing-card">🔑 Login</Link>
        <Link to="/register" className="landing-card">📝 Register</Link>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

---

**src/components/Layout/LandingPage.css**
```css
.landing-container {
  max-width: 900px;
  margin: 40px auto;
  padding: 32px;
  background: #fff;
  border-radius: 16px;
  box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
  text-align: center;
}

.landing-links {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  justify-content: center;
  gap: 24px;
  margin-top: 32px;
}

.landing-card {
  display: block;
  width: 180px;
  padding: 24px 0;
  background: #f0f4ff;
  border-radius: 12px;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  font-weight: 500;
  color: #1a237e;
  text-decoration: none;
  box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(26,35,126,0.08);
  transition: background 0.2s, box-shadow 0.2s;
}
.landing-card:hover {
  background: #e3eaff;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(26,35,126,0.16);
}
```

---

**Update your router (App.js):**
```javascript
import LandingPage from "./components/Layout/LandingPage";
// ...other imports...

function App() {
  return (
    <BrowserRouter>
      {/* <Navbar /> */}
      <Routes>
        <Route path="/" element={<LandingPage />} />
        {/* ...other routes... */}
      </Routes>
    </BrowserRouter>
  );
}
```

---

**Result:**  
- You’ll have a modern, attractive landing page with big clickable cards for each service.
- You can further enhance it with images, animations, or a UI library.

Let me know if you want a version using Material-UI or want to add more features!

